		{"id":"exegesis","type":"text","text":"## Scripture · begin with the actual source\nPlanted has approved curriculum. The vault records Session 0 and the Session 1 title, “In the Beginning, a Garden.”\n\nChoose the next session and read its supplied text/material; do not invent the absent sequence.","x":30,"y":70,"width":560,"height":360,"color":"#4A90D9"},
		{"id":"synthesis","type":"text","text":"## Theology · synthesis from the text\nHow does the supplied passage illuminate Christ and the biblical story?\n\nKeep observation, interpretation, and proposal distinct. Use actual Notion/source notes; do not infer the four unrecorded frameworks.","x":710,"y":70,"width":560,"height":360,"color":"#9B72CF"},
		{"id":"formation","type":"text","text":"## Formation · approved goal\nBelong to God’s people · behold and follow Jesus · grow in faith · plant seeds of hope in others.\n\nTranslate the goal into concrete invitations for this session.","x":1390,"y":70,"width":560,"height":360,"color":"#65A86B"},
		{"id":"design","type":"text","text":"## Teaching Flow · Planted\nWorking envelope: 6:30–8:00 PM\n20 community/check-in + about 60 study/discussion + 10 closing.\n\nRetain approved Scripture, story, experience, conversation, practice, prayer/worship, and community.\n\nThe Collective two-block pattern is not automatically applied here.","x":2070,"y":70,"width":560,"height":340,"color":"#D6B34B"},
		{"id":"discussion","type":"text","text":"## Discussion · develop from the passage\nWhat helps people notice the text, behold Christ, and respond honestly?\n\nKeep room for newcomers and honest questions; no pressure to disclose.","x":2070,"y":440,"width":560,"height":310,"color":"#D96B6B"},
		{"id":"production","type":"text","text":"## Resource Output · Paul develops\nSession presentation slides + participant handout/notes\n\nPlanted session notes may be 4+ pages where depth requires. Apply the shared Groups style; inspect exported pages/slides.","x":2750,"y":70,"width":560,"height":360,"color":"#9098A1"},
		{"id":"source-notes","type":"text","text":"## Open source details\nActual next-session source / Notion version\nTen movements / five chapters / twelve-session mapping\nFour remaining frameworks\n\nApproved curriculum stays approved; local source gaps remain named.","x":30,"y":710,"width":560,"height":330,"color":"#4A90D9"},
		{"id":"next","type":"text","text":"## Next action · Paul\nLink the next approved session source and Notion version, then develop one session master through the five stages.","x":2070,"y":800,"width":560,"height":250,"color":"#D6B34B"},
		{"id":"session-template","type":"file","file":"Groups Ministry/10 Templates/Records/Curriculum Session.md","x":1390,"y":480,"width":560,"height":180,"color":"#9098A1"},
		{"id":"master-link","type":"text","text":"## Link the actual phase 03 master\nAfter Paul confirms the phase 02 synthesis/goals/outline, create the actual gathering master in 03 Develop Content.\n\nKeep this brief/map here in phase 02; link the real master and editable resources. Preserve input provenance.","x":1390,"y":720,"width":560,"height":310,"color":"#65A86B"},
		{"id":"review","type":"text","text":"## Review and release handoffs\nPaul confirms phase 02 direction and reviews actual phase 03 editable content.\n\nResource Producer verifies actual exports. Paul’s final review precedes phase 04 library promotion. Record actual response/date/version here in the project brief.","x":2750,"y":480,"width":560,"height":310,"color":"#9098A1"},
